From 588b5b69c0cccd1ed153e22b2c20ac7af4176c67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 12:17:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: author D17 movement catalog and deterministic GUIDE
 routine validator

Phase 1 (Days 5-6) backend work that has no dependency on physical Fire TV
hardware or the Android toolchain, per D30/architecture: the physical-device
gate blocks P2/P3 device validation only, not this work.

- shared/movement-catalog/catalog.json: 45 hand-authored movements across
  the exact composition in ARCHITECTURE_MVP_PLAN.md section 7.2 (6 warmup,
  12 mobility, 8 light-strength, 10 stretch, 5 breathing, 4 relaxation).
  Every entry satisfies SAFE-030 (low-to-moderate, bodyweight, no equipment)
  and SAFE-034 by construction (no plyometric/high-impact/breath-holding/
  spinal-loading/equipment content). All entries are SEATED or
  STANDING_SUPPORTED (exceeds the SAFE-037 "roughly half" floor).
  contraindicationTags are the join key to confirmed Precaution.blocksMovementTags
  (SAFE-032).

- backend/guardrail/routine_validator.py: the five deterministic checks from
  section 7.3 (catalog membership, precaution-filter enforcement, SAFE-811
  warmup/cooldown structure, PROD-121 duration tolerance, per-movement
  min/max bounds). Independent of any prompt or AI provider (SAFE-921);
  the GUIDE model is only ever allowed to emit catalog IDs + durations,
  never movement text (D13), and this is what turns that into PASS/FAIL.
  Fails closed on any unresolved/malformed input (SAFE-920).

- backend/tests/test_routine_validator.py: 18 new tests -- catalog
  authoring invariants (composition, no HIGH intensity, no equipment,
  unique ids, resolvable gentler-variant refs) plus one test per
  deterministic check, including the case that matters most: a movement
  the precaution filter excluded still fails validation even if a model
  ignored the filtered catalog and returned it anyway.

Verification: 25/25 backend tests pass (7 pre-existing P4 tests unaffected
+ 18 new). No secrets, no clinical/patient content, no unrelated files
touched. P1 physical-device validation and P2/P3 remain explicitly PENDING
-- unaffected and untouched by this change.

